@startuml Authentication Flow

' ============================================================================
' Authentication Flow Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows how Bearer Token authentication works in the API.
' All endpoints (except /health) require a valid token in the Authorization header.
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor DarkRed
    ActorBorderColor DarkRed
    LifeLineBorderColor DarkRed
    ParticipantBackgroundColor MistyRose
    ParticipantBorderColor DarkRed
}

title Bearer Token Authentication Flow

actor "API Client" as Client
participant "FastAPI\nMiddleware" as API
participant "HTTPBearer\n(FastAPI Security)" as Bearer
participant "verify_token()\n(auth.py)" as Auth
participant "Settings\n(config.py)" as Config
participant "Router\nEndpoint" as Router

' ============================================================================
' Successful Authentication
' ============================================================================
== Successful Authentication ==

Client -> API : Request with header:\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>

API -> Bearer : Extract token from header
Bearer -> Bearer : Validate header format\n"Bearer <token>"

alt Invalid Header Format
    Bearer --> Client : 403 Forbidden\n"Not authenticated"
else Valid Format
    Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)

    Auth -> Config : Get API_TOKENS\nfrom environment
    Config --> Auth : ["test-token-123", "test-token-456"]

    Auth -> Auth : Check if token in valid_tokens

    alt Token Valid
        Auth --> Bearer : Return token (success)
        Bearer --> API : Token validated
        API -> Router : Process request
        Router --> Client : 200 OK (response data)
    else Token Invalid
        Auth --> Client : 401 Unauthorized\n"Invalid authentication token"
    end
end

' ============================================================================
' Missing Token
' ============================================================================
== Missing Token ==

Client -> API : Request without\nAuthorization header
API -> Bearer : No token found
Bearer --> Client : 403 Forbidden\n"Not authenticated"

' ============================================================================
' Notes
' ============================================================================

note right of Config
  **Token Configuration:**
  Environment variable: API_TOKENS
  Default: ["test-token-123", "test-token-456"]

  Format: JSON array of strings
  Set in docker-compose.yml
end note

note right of Auth
  **Security Features:**
  - Simple token comparison
  - No token expiration (stateless)
  - Multiple valid tokens supported

  **For Production:**
  - Use JWT tokens
  - Add token expiration
  - Implement refresh tokens
end note

note bottom of Client
  **Usage Example:**
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer test-token-123" \
       http://localhost:8000/experiments
end note

@enduml
